  "vibe": "A CRT indigo void (#14122b) lit by phosphor green (#6ef06e), magenta (#ff4fd8) and cyan (#4fd8ff). Press Start 2P sets small slammed caps at 64–110px; VT323 does the body. The world is an actual attract-mode loop: twenty-two square stars stepping in quantised jumps, five invader sprites cycling two hand-drawn pixel frames at 1.6Hz and marching 30px sideways, a translucent scanline band sweeping the full height, a green cannon sliding on a sine at the bottom and two shots — one white, one magenta — climbing away from it. Roll and skew are pinned to zero and the camera alternates strictly pushL / pushR, so nothing ever tilts off the pixel grid. Terminal code, key-press cursor, flip swipe, bar meters. For games, dev tools, launches and arcade nostalgia.",
